From a4d4fe511565517e2e67584383dc991cca172bc3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 18 Nov 2026 21:36:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: imx111: Don't shorten a mode's frame below its
 default length

The vertical blanking range starts at 16 lines for every mode, but the
sensor does not stream at every frame length that allows. In the
3280x2464 mode it delivers two or three frames and then stops at 16, 20
or 24 lines of blanking, at any exposure, while 26 lines (the mode's
default frame length of 2490 lines) and more stream normally. libcamera's
AGC now controls the blanking, and asking for a frame rate the mode
cannot reach clamps it to the minimum, which stalls the stream.

Each mode's default frame length is the one its register set was made
with. Use it as the shortest frame the mode allows: the blanking may
grow from the default, for longer exposures, but not shrink below it.

Signed-off-by: Patrick Quinn <patrick.jm.quinn@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c b/drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c
index d0a72f3..96b0c44 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/imx111.c
@@ -89,7 +89,6 @@
 /* frame timing registers */
 #define IMX111_VERTICAL_TOTAL_LENGTH		CCI_REG16(0x0340)
 #define IMX111_VTL_MAX				0x09d8
-#define IMX111_VBLANK_MIN			16
 #define IMX111_HORIZONTAL_TOTAL_LENGTH		CCI_REG16(0x0342)
 #define IMX111_HTL_MAX				0x0dd0
 #define IMX111_HBLANK_MIN			16
@@ -932,7 +931,7 @@ static int imx111_init_controls(struct imx111 *sensor)
 		sensor->vflip->flags |= V4L2_CTRL_FLAG_MODIFY_LAYOUT;
 
 	sensor->vblank = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_VBLANK,
-					   IMX111_VBLANK_MIN,
+					   mode->vtl_def - mode->height,
 					   IMX111_VTL_MAX - mode->height, 1,
 					   mode->vtl_def - mode->height);
 	sensor->hblank = v4l2_ctrl_new_std(hdl, ops, V4L2_CID_HBLANK,
@@ -1150,7 +1149,7 @@ static int imx111_set_format(struct v4l2_subdev *sd,
 			return ret;
 
 		ret = __v4l2_ctrl_modify_range(sensor->vblank,
-					       IMX111_VBLANK_MIN,
+					       mode->vtl_def - mode->height,
 					       IMX111_VTL_MAX - mode->height,
 					       1,
 					       mode->vtl_def - mode->height);
